Package: stepmetrics
Type: Package
Title: Step Detection Algorithms and Step and Cadence Metrics for Wearable Data
Version: 1.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jairo H", "Migueles", 
           email = "jairo@jhmigueles.com", 
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Elroy J", "Aguiar", role = "fnd", 
           comment = "Funding and data support"),
    person("University of Alabama", "", role = "fnd"))
Description: Open-source implementations of step-detection algorithms for raw
    accelerometer and gyroscope data, and functions to calculate step- and
    cadence-based metrics from them or from step counts of other devices.
    Raw files from 'Axivity', 'GENEActiv', 'Parmay Matrix', 'ActiGraph' and
    'Movisens' devices are read whole in a common format that keeps the
    gyroscope and the time of every sample, which suits laboratory
    protocols. Every algorithm returns the time of each step, can run on
    multi-day recordings inside R package 'GGIR'
    <https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR> as an external function, and can be
    validated against a reference with the same matching criterion. Step
    counts per epoch from 'ActiGraph' (CSV and AGD), 'Fitbit' (CSV) and 'GGIR'
    output are also supported, with automatic handling of epoch lengths from
    1 to 60 seconds. Metrics include total steps, cadence peaks, minutes and
    steps in predefined cadence bands, and time and steps in
    moderate-to-vigorous physical activity (MVPA). Methods and thresholds are
    informed by the literature, e.g.,
    Tudor-Locke and Rowe (2012) <doi:10.2165/11599170-000000000-00000>,
    Barreira et al. (2012) <doi:10.1249/MSS.0b013e318254f2a3>,
    and Tudor-Locke et al. (2018) <doi:10.1136/bjsports-2017-097628>.
    The package record is also available on Zenodo (2023) <doi:10.5281/zenodo.7858094>.
